  "H1 seasonality: the miner has hour-of-day (t.hour_utc, t.min_to_funding) but no weekday feature, so weekday d / weekend x side x template was screened on both grids with the miner's datasets and statistics (192 rules): best market-excess t 2.50 (Monday short, 1d grid, 2024 t -0.98), nothing validated, no lab",
  "result of H0: 104,871 rules, bar 4.81; 3 rules passed, all LONG after a sharp drop with the 4 ATR catastrophic stop and a 24h time exit (no hour-of-day feature in any of the 16 kept rules): a market-wide OI flush (rcbde21f7) and two coin capitulations with mean-reverting 15m bars (r1458e9d8, rc899282d)",
  "lab: rc899282d alone passes every TRAIN condition (t_day 4.89 vs 4.81); the OI flush rule fails (t_day 2.45: 2024 trades cluster on few days, 2022 has almost no top-trader data), the ADX variant fails (4.48), and the union of the three fails (3.54): the candidate is the single rule"
